== no_variables
error[Z0406]: `heatmap` needs `vars`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:3
  |
2 | d.heatmap()
  |   ^^^^^^^ `vars` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `data.heatmap(vars)`

== one_variable
error[Z0401]: `heatmap` shows the correlations of variables with one another, so it needs two or more, but this is one
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | d.heatmap([a])
  |           ^^^ fewer than two variables
  |
  = help: list the variables in brackets, in the order they are to stand, as in `heatmap([wage, educ, exper])`

== a_variable_alone_without_brackets
error[Z0401]: `heatmap` shows the correlations of variables with one another, so it needs two or more, but this is one
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | d.heatmap(a)
  |           ^ fewer than two variables
  |
  = help: list the variables in brackets, in the order they are to stand, as in `heatmap([wage, educ, exper])`

== a_variable_twice
error[Z0401]: `heatmap` is given `a` twice
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | d.heatmap([a, b, a])
  |           ^^^^^^^^^ one variable, twice
  |
  = help: a variable stands once in a heat map; leave the second out

== a_variable_of_text
error[Z0401]: `heatmap` shows correlations, which are of numbers, but `name` is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | d.heatmap([a, name])
  |           ^^^^^^^^^ `name` is not numeric
  |
  = help: leave `name` out, or give a variable of numbers: a Float, an Int or a Bool; `d.describe()` lists the types of the variables

== a_variable_not_there
error[Z0101]: no variable `bb` in `d`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | d.heatmap([a, bb])
  |           ^^^^^^^ not a variable of d
  |
  = help: did you mean `b`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"b"`

== a_variable_in_another_case
error[Z0102]: no variable `B` in `d`; names are case-sensitive
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | d.heatmap([a, B])
  |           ^^^^^^ differs only in case from `b`
  |
  = help: write `b`

== panels_which_it_does_not_take
error[Z0404]: `heatmap` has no argument called `by`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:19
  |
2 | d.heatmap([a, b], by: name)
  |                   ^^ unknown argument
  |
  = help: usage: `data.heatmap(vars)`

== a_heat_map_of_a_plot
error[Z0401]: `heatmap` cannot be called on a Plot
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | d.plot(x: a).heatmap([a, b])
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is a Plot
  |
  = help: `heatmap` takes a Frame first; `x.heatmap(...)` is `heatmap(x, ...)`
